<section class="gg-about-human-hero">
  <div class="gg-container gg-about-human-grid">
    <div>
      <span class="gg-kicker">About Goal Grower</span>
      <h1>This app started with a simple feeling.</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="gg-about-note">
      <p>
        It is hard to stay motivated when your goals feel like chores.
        Goal Grower is being built to make progress feel more alive, more visual,
        and easier to return to after imperfect days.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="gg-about-letter">
  <div class="gg-container">
    <div class="gg-letter-panel">
      <span class="gg-kicker">A note from the builder</span>

      <h2>I wanted goals to feel less like pressure and more like care.</h2>

      <p>
        Most goal apps are lists, streaks, charts, and numbers. Those can help,
        but they can also make progress feel cold. Goal Grower is different
        because each goal becomes something living.
      </p>

      <p>
        If you show up, your plant grows. If you miss a day, the goal is still
        there waiting for you to come back. The point is not perfection. The
        point is returning.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="gg-about-values">
  <div class="gg-container">
    <div class="gg-about-value">
      <span>01</span>
      <h3>Progress should be visible.</h3>
      <p>Your effort should feel real, not hidden inside a checklist.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="gg-about-value">
      <span>02</span>
      <h3>Growth should allow imperfect days.</h3>
      <p>The app is built around returning, not pretending every day is perfect.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="gg-about-value">
      <span>03</span>
      <h3>Goals should feel personal.</h3>
      <p>Your garden becomes a small reflection of the life you are building.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="gg-about-builder">
  <div class="gg-container gg-about-builder-grid">
    <div>
      <span class="gg-kicker light">Built in progress</span>
      <h2>Goal Grower is still growing too.</h2>
    </div>

    <div>
      <p>
        The app currently supports goal tracking, personal gardens, and shared
        gardens in beta. Testing, feedback, and support help turn it into a more
        polished, useful, and motivating app.
      </p>

      <div class="gg-hero-actions">
        <a href="/pages/contact" class="gg-btn">Become a Tester</a>
        <a href="/pages/support" class="gg-btn-soft light-btn">Support Development</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

